course: dictionary
lesson: 6334
title: Mound: a small hill or a big heap
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A mound is a raised pile, such as a small hill or a heap of earth, stones or other things. Context tells you which kind of mound is meant.
explain: «Red wood ants bite and spray acid to defend their nest mounds, which can hold hundreds of thousands of ants.» A nest that holds hundreds of thousands of ants is a raised pile of earth, not a tiny bump, so the clues point to a pile.
explain: «A chimp pushes a stripped grass stem into a termite mound.» The stick goes into the mound, so the mound is a solid, raised structure. Swap in your meaning: "a chimp pushes a stick into a raised heap" still makes sense.
fact: A mound is a small hill or a pile of earth, stones or other things.
fact: «A mound of homework» means a big heap of homework.
fact: A burial mound is a mound built long ago over a grave.
fact: Ants and termites build mounds, and moles leave molehills.
fact: In baseball, the mound is the raised spot where the pitcher stands.
exercise: «Red wood ants defend their nest mounds, which can hold hundreds of thousands of ants.» What is a mound here? | A running track | A small pond | A type of sweet | *A raised pile of earth that holds an ant nest
exercise: «She has a mound of homework to do tonight.» What does mound mean? | *A big heap | Flat, empty field | A friendly dog | Tiny seed
exercise: Which of these is a burial mound? | A bag of flour | *A raised hill built long ago over a grave | A new swimming pool | A shop window
test: «Giant anteaters rip open hard termite mounds with their long front claws.» What is being ripped open? | Long grass | *Hard termite mounds | Soft sand | A fallen tree
test: Where does a baseball pitcher stand? | In the dugout | First base | Home plate | *On the mound
exam: «Next door the chimpanzees poke sticks into a fake termite mound to fish out honey.» What does mound most likely mean? | *A raised heap of earth | A sort of stick | A type of tree | A kind of honey jar
